                <pb facs="0778" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg674"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>No official record of the conversation at this meeting has been found. According
                    to Leahy, p. 213, the conversation dealt
                    with (1) the allocation of forces for the operation against the Andaman Islands
                    or alternatively against Rhodes, and (2) the choice of zones of occupation in
                    Germany as between the United States and the United Kingdom. With regard to the
                    first topic, Leahy states that Roosevelt insisted on the Andaman Islands
                    operation and emphasized that promises made to Chiang should be fully carried out. With respect to the second
                    topic, Churchill and Eden argued for British occupation of the
                    northwestern zone in Germany. See also <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg253">p. 253</ref>; <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg688">p. 688</ref>; and Churchill, pp. 408–409.</p>
                <p>The list of those present is derived from the Log, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>,). 656. Neither Churchill
                    nor Leahy mentions Hopkins’ presence, and Leahy refers to those present at the meeting as
                    a party of four. Roosevelt acted as
                    host.</p>
            </div>
